---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import PhotoHero from "../components/PhotoHero.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import dignityPhoto from "../assets/images/dignity-moment.jpg";
import workshopPhoto from "../assets/images/workshop-craft.jpg";
import hubExterior from "../assets/images/humanity-hub-exterior.jpg";
import { getTeamMembers, getPartners, getSupporters, getPressMentions, urlFor } from "../lib/sanity";

const team = await getTeamMembers();
const partners = await getPartners();
// One lead partner, shown first and larger (the 2 September review: Woolworths at the top, with a
// larger banner). Set with "Lead partner" in the Studio - currently Woolworths, using their public
// wordmark pending their OK (q30 on the status page); with none set, nothing changes. Partners with
// a website become link cards.
const featuredPartner = partners.find((p) => p.featured);
const otherPartners = featuredPartner ? partners.filter((p) => p !== featuredPartner) : partners;
const FeaturedTag = featuredPartner?.url ? "a" : "div";
const supporters = await getSupporters();
const pressMentions = await getPressMentions();
---

<Layout heroOverlay title="Who we are, and the Humanity Hub" description="Souper Troopers' mission, values and approach, and the Humanity Hub - the service centre in Woodstock, Cape Town where the work actually happens.">
	{/* The shared photo hero (design brief, 24 September). The building, not people: consent to show
	    anyone (q19) is unsettled, and it is what the opening line names. Cropped from the right only,
	    so the painted 66 stays in frame. alt="" because it is a backdrop here; Contact carries the
	    described version of the same photo. */}
	<PhotoHero image={hubExterior} position="left center">
		<h1>Who We Are</h1>
		<p>
			At the Humanity Hub in Woodstock, Cape Town, we help people move from life on the street
			to independence, through the CAST programme. Est. 2014.
		</p>
	</PhotoHero>

	<section class="section wrap">
		{/* Section titles on this page say what the section is; the old chips above them did that,
		    and the titles repeated the paragraph's first line (changed 2026-09-14). */}
		{/* `statement` is the centred, larger variant (Layout.astro) - kept for this one section, which
		    the user liked for how playful it looked, with the glow on the word that matters. */}
		<div class="section-intro statement">
			<h2>Our <span class="glow-word">mission</span></h2>
			<p>
				Every person deserves dignity, and with the right support, anyone can rebuild their future.
				That belief drives everything we do - from a first conversation on the street to a first
				pay cheque.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	{/* A plain section since 2026-09-24 (design brief phase 2): the teal-red gradient band behind it
	    is retired site-wide. */}
	<section class="section wrap">
		<div class="section-intro">
			<h2>How we began</h2>
			{/* The opening line stays in view; the rest of Kerry's origin story opens on click rather
			    than being cut - the words stay in the page for search and for anyone who wants them. */}
			<p>
				In June 2014, Kerry Hoffman spent a day sharing soup and sandwiches with people living on
				the street.
			</p>
			<details class="card-more">
				<summary><span class="card-more-show">More</span><span class="card-more-hide">Less</span><span class="visually-hidden"> about how we began</span></summary>
				<div>
					<p>
						That relaxed social gathering - and the regular monthly events that followed for the
						next five years - helped us understand the complexity of homelessness and the
						inadequacies of existing interventions. Those early years cemented Souper Troopers in
						the social capital of the streets, and taught us that every person has their own story
						and needs individualised support to move forward.
					</p>
				</div>
			</details>
			<p>Kerry still leads Souper Troopers today - <a href="#team">meet the team</a>.</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section wrap">
		<div class="section-intro">
			<h2>How we work</h2>
			{/* "Dignity, love and respect" is the organisation's motto (the bracelet, the CAST steps,
			    the homepage). It was this section's title until 2026-09-14 and nothing else on the page
			    says it, so it moved into the first line rather than going. */}
			<p>
				Everything rests on dignity, love and respect. Every beneficiary is seen as human first -
				before being homeless - and three principles hold that in place.
			</p>
		</div>
		<div class="grid grid-3">
			<div class="card">
				<h3>A hand up, not a handout</h3>
				<p>Support is offered to a person, not administered to a case.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="card">
				<h3>Relationships, not transactions</h3>
				<p>
					We meet people where they are, and we keep showing up - which is what makes the harder
					conversations possible later.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div class="card">
				<h3>No two journeys are the same</h3>
				<p>Each person's plan is built with them, around what they actually need.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
		<p><a href="/our-work">See the full CAST journey &rarr;</a></p>
	</section>

	<section id="humanity-hub" class="section wrap">
		<div class="grid grid-2" style="align-items:center;">
			<div class="section-intro">
				<h2>The Humanity Hub</h2>
				<p>
					Our service centre at 66 Newmarket Street, Woodstock, is where all of this happens - a
					permanent address in a life where very little is permanent. Somewhere to be expected.
					Somewhere to come back to.
				</p>
				<p>
					Everything from a shower and a hot meal to counselling, ID documents, and job-readiness
					support runs out of the Hub. <a href="/our-work">See what that support looks like</a> on
					Our Work.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div class="figure shimmer-up">
				<Image
					src={dignityPhoto}
					alt="A member of the Souper Troopers community smiling"
					width={800} widths={[400, 800]}
					sizes="(min-width: 700px) 500px, 100vw"
					onload="this.classList.add('is-loaded')"
				/>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section wrap">
		<div class="grid grid-2" style="align-items:center;">
			<div class="figure shimmer-up">
				<Image
					src={workshopPhoto}
					alt="A Souper Squad skills workshop, making African Worry Dolls together"
					width={800} widths={[400, 800]}
					sizes="(min-width: 700px) 500px, 100vw"
					onload="this.classList.add('is-loaded')"
				/>
			</div>
			<div class="section-intro">
				<h2>A business, not just a charity</h2>
				{/* The Squad's list of activities lives on Our Work (the services cards); repeating it here
				    word for word was the About/Our Work overlap found in the 2026-09-14 repetition pass. */}
				<p>
					More than twenty Troopers earn a stipend through the Souper Squad. It is real work, with
					real income, building a real CV.
				</p>
				<p>
					What they make - Troopers Coffee and African Worry Dolls&trade; - is sold through Shmiley
					(Pty) Ltd, our own social enterprise. The income creates the jobs and reduces our reliance
					on donor funding - so <a href="/shop">buying something from the shop</a> is itself a way
					of supporting the work.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section id="team" class="section wrap">
		<div class="section-intro">
			<h2>Meet the team</h2>
		</div>
		<div class="team-grid">
			{team.map((person) => (
				<div class="card" style="text-align:center; align-items:center;">
					{person.photo && (
						<div
							class="team-photo blur-up"
							style={person.photoLqip ? `background-image:url(${person.photoLqip})` : undefined}
						>
							<img
								src={urlFor(person.photo).width(300).height(300).fit("crop").auto("format").url()}
								alt={person.name}
								width="120"
								height="120"
								loading="lazy"
								onload="this.classList.add('is-loaded')"
							/>
						</div>
					)}
					<h3>{person.name}</h3>
					<p>{person.role}</p>
					{person.bio && <p class="team-bio">{person.bio}</p>}
				</div>
			))}
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="dark-band">
		<div class="wrap">
			<div class="section-intro">
				<h2>Partners &amp; supporters</h2>
				<p>These businesses and organisations choose to partner with and support Souper Troopers. Open one to see how.</p>
			</div>
			{featuredPartner && (
				<FeaturedTag
					class="card partner-featured"
					{...(featuredPartner.url ? { href: featuredPartner.url, target: "_blank", rel: "noopener" } : {})}
				>
					{featuredPartner.logo && (
						<div class:list={["partner-logo-frame", featuredPartner.logoOnDark && "on-dark"]}>
							<img class="partner-logo" src={urlFor(featuredPartner.logo).width(600).url()} alt={featuredPartner.name} width="320" height="120" loading="lazy" />
						</div>
					)}
					<div class="partner-featured-text">
						<h3>{featuredPartner.name}</h3>
						<p>{featuredPartner.blurb}</p>
						{featuredPartner.url && <span class="partner-visit">Visit their site &rarr;</span>}
					</div>
				</FeaturedTag>
			)}
			{/* A logo wall: the brands are what the section is for ("credible brands backing
			    everything", the 2 September review), so each tile shows logo and name, and what the
			    partner gives opens on click. <details>, so the words stay in the page for search.
			    The logo's alt is empty because the name sits right beside it - otherwise every tile is
			    announced twice. A partner's website link lives inside the opened tile: the tile is
			    itself a control, and a link can't nest inside one. */}
			<ul class="partner-wall">
				{otherPartners.map((partner) => (
					<li>
						<details class="partner-tile">
							<summary>
								{partner.logo && (
									<span class:list={["partner-logo-frame", partner.logoOnDark && "on-dark"]}>
										<img
											class="partner-logo"
											src={urlFor(partner.logo).width(300).url()}
											alt=""
											width="96"
											height="72"
											loading="lazy"
										/>
									</span>
								)}
								<h3>{partner.name}</h3>
							</summary>
							<div class="partner-tile-more">
								<p>{partner.blurb}</p>
								{partner.url && <a href={partner.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visit their site &rarr;</a>}
							</div>
						</details>
					</li>
				))}
			</ul>

			{supporters.length > 0 && (
				<details class="supporters">
					<summary><h3>And many more who give goods, services, space, and time</h3></summary>
					<ul class="supporter-list">
						{supporters.map((supporter) => (
							<li>
								{supporter.url ? (
									<a href={supporter.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{supporter.name}</a>
								) : (
									supporter.name
								)}
								{supporter.note && <span class="supporter-note"> - {supporter.note}</span>}
							</li>
						))}
					</ul>
				</details>
			)}
		</div>
	</section>

	{pressMentions.length > 0 && (
		<section class="section wrap">
			<div class="section-intro">
				<h2>In the news</h2>
			</div>
			<div class="grid grid-3">
				{pressMentions.map((mention) => (
					<div class="card">
						<span class="press-publication">{mention.publication}</span>
						<h3>{mention.headline}</h3>
						{mention.url && (
							<a href={mention.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read the article &rarr;</a>
						)}
					</div>
				))}
			</div>
		</section>
	)}

</Layout>

<style>
	/* The lead partner: the same white card, full width, logo larger beside the words. */
	.partner-featured {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: auto 1fr;
		align-items: center;
		gap: var(--space-8);
		padding: var(--space-8);
		color: var(--st-ink);
		text-decoration: none;
	}

	/* Wide enough for a wordmark: Woolworths' is 6.5:1, so a 220px frame left it 34px tall. */
	.partner-featured .partner-logo-frame {
		width: 320px;
		max-width: 100%;
		height: 120px;
	}

	.partner-featured h3 {
		margin: 0 0 var(--space-2);
		font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 2.6vw, 1.9rem);
	}

	.partner-featured p {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: 1.05rem;
	}

	/* The link cue: teal-dark and underlined, the site's mark for "you can act on this". */
	.partner-visit {
		margin-top: auto;
		padding-top: var(--space-2);
		font-size: 0.9rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		color: var(--st-teal-dark);
		text-decoration: underline;
		text-underline-offset: 3px;
	}

	@media (max-width: 700px) {
		.partner-featured {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			gap: var(--space-4);
			padding: var(--space-6);
		}
	}

	/* How we began sits on the teal-to-red band, where the site's teal-dark "More" would vanish.
	   White, like the band's text around it. */
	/* The logo wall. Flex rather than a grid, like .team-grid, so a part-filled last row centres
	   itself: the partner count comes from Sanity and will change when Kerry revises the list.
	   190px tiles give five to a row at the 1100px cap. align-items: flex-start so an opened tile
	   grows on its own instead of stretching its whole row. */
	.partner-wall {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		justify-content: center;
		align-items: flex-start;
		gap: var(--space-4);
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0;
		list-style: none;
	}

	.partner-wall > li {
		flex: 0 1 190px;
	}

	.partner-tile {
		border-radius: var(--radius);
		background: var(--st-white);
		color: var(--st-ink);
	}

	.partner-tile > summary {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		align-items: center;
		gap: var(--space-2);
		padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-3) var(--space-3);
		text-align: center;
		list-style: none;
		cursor: pointer;
	}

	.partner-tile > summary::-webkit-details-marker {
		display: none;
	}

	/* Two lines reserved for every name, so closed tiles are all one height and the chevrons line
	   up across a row - "Capital International Group" wraps, "CNC Products" doesn't. */
	.partner-tile > summary h3 {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
		min-height: 2.6em;
		margin: 0;
		font-size: 0.95rem;
		line-height: 1.3;
	}

	/* The cue that a tile opens: a teal-dark chevron, the site's colour for things you can act on. */
	.partner-tile > summary::after {
		content: "";
		width: 7px;
		height: 7px;
		margin-top: 2px;
		border-right: 2px solid var(--st-teal-dark);
		border-bottom: 2px solid var(--st-teal-dark);
		transform: rotate(45deg);
		transition: transform 120ms ease;
	}

	.partner-tile[open] > summary::after {
		margin-top: 6px;
		transform: rotate(-135deg);
	}

	.partner-tile > summary:focus-visible {
		outline: 3px solid var(--st-teal);
		outline-offset: 2px;
		border-radius: var(--radius);
	}

	.partner-wall .partner-logo-frame {
		width: 96px;
		height: 72px;
	}

	.partner-tile-more {
		padding: 0 var(--space-4) var(--space-4);
		font-size: 0.88rem;
		text-align: center;
	}

	.partner-tile-more p {
		margin: 0;
		color: rgba(36, 35, 43, 0.8);
	}

	.partner-tile-more a {
		display: inline-block;
		margin-top: var(--space-2);
		font-weight: 700;
		color: var(--st-teal-dark);
	}

	/* At phone width the longest names ("Capital International Group") take three lines, so three
	   are reserved there - otherwise the tiles in a pair differ by ~19px. */
	@media (max-width: 480px) {
		.partner-wall > li {
			flex-basis: 150px;
		}

		.partner-tile > summary h3 {
			min-height: 3.9em;
		}
	}

	/* The supporters list, closed by default behind its own heading. White and underlined on the ink
	   band - teal-dark there is 3.3:1. */
	.supporters > summary {
		display: inline-flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 0.5em;
		color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85);
		list-style: none;
		cursor: pointer;
	}

	.supporters > summary::-webkit-details-marker {
		display: none;
	}

	.supporters > summary h3 {
		margin: 0;
		color: inherit;
		text-decoration: underline;
		text-underline-offset: 3px;
	}

	.supporters > summary::after {
		content: "";
		flex-shrink: 0;
		width: 7px;
		height: 7px;
		border-right: 2px solid currentColor;
		border-bottom: 2px solid currentColor;
		transform: rotate(45deg) translate(-2px, -2px);
		transition: transform 120ms ease;
	}

	.supporters[open] > summary::after {
		transform: rotate(-135deg) translate(-1px, -1px);
	}

	.supporters[open] .supporter-list {
		margin-top: var(--space-4);
	}

	@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
		.partner-tile > summary::after,
		.supporters > summary::after {
			transition: none;
		}
	}

</style>
